<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata minClientVersion="5.3">
    <!-- Package id must be unique on nuget.org; keep it stable once published -->
    <id>VikashKumar.XrmToolBox.PluginFailureCorrelationExplorer</id>
    <!-- Keep in sync with <Version> in PluginFailureCorrelationExplorer.csproj (format 1.YYYY.M.rev) -->
    <version>1.2026.10.1</version>
    <title>Plugin Failure Correlation Explorer</title>
    <authors>Vikash Kumar</authors>
    <owners>vikashkumar669</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/vikashkumar669/XrmTools/tree/main/PluginFailureCorrelationExplorer</projectUrl>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/vikashkumar669/XrmTools.git" branch="main" />
    <!-- Icon by URL only (same as the other tools): GitHub serves it as image/png. When the icon is embedded,
         nuget.org sometimes stores it as application/octet-stream, which the XrmToolBox portal rejects ("Logo Url is not valid"). -->
    <iconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vikashkumar669/XrmTools/main/PluginFailureCorrelationExplorer/src/PluginFailureCorrelationExplorer/Resources/icon128.png</iconUrl>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <description>Plugin Failure Correlation Explorer correlates Dataverse plug-in failures, identifies recurring exceptions, analyzes execution patterns and generates evidence-based diagnostic reports from plug-in trace logs. Failures are grouped by a normalized exception fingerprint that keeps generic messages from different plug-ins apart. Every relationship between traces carries an explicit evidence level (exact request match, same causal chain, suspected parent/child, heuristic, same pattern) and the signals that produced it. A rule engine produces findings that separate observed facts, calculated metrics, correlation evidence and possible explanations, with recommended investigation steps. Compare with a previous period or a saved aggregate snapshot to find new or increasing failures and performance regressions. Export a standalone HTML report, JSON or CSV, with optional redaction of GUIDs, e-mail addresses and URL query strings; credentials are always removed. Read-only: never writes to Dataverse.</description>
    <summary>Correlate Dataverse plugin failures, identify recurring exceptions, analyze execution patterns, and generate actionable diagnostic reports.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>1.2026.10.1: First release.
- Retrieve plug-in trace logs with server-side filters (date range, exception presence, message, table, plug-in type, correlation ID, request ID, minimum duration), paging, a result limit and cancel
- Exception fingerprinting with documented, unit-tested normalization rules and custom rules
- Evidence-based correlation: exact request, same causal chain, suspected parent/child, heuristic and same-pattern links, each explained
- Performance analysis against sync/async thresholds with average, median and nearest-rank 95th percentile when the sample allows
- Nine diagnostic rules (recurring, high frequency, slow, hotspot, incomplete evidence, new/increasing, regression, failure chains, suspected recursion)
- Trend comparison with the previous period or a saved aggregate snapshot, refused with a reason when not like-for-like
- Standalone HTML, JSON and CSV exports with redaction; credentials always removed</releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright © Vikash Kumar 2026</copyright>
    <!-- "XrmToolBox" must be the first tag for the tool to appear in the XrmToolBox Tool Library -->
    <tags>XrmToolBox PluginTrace TraceLog Correlation Diagnostics Plugins Exceptions Performance Troubleshooting Dataverse Dynamics365 PowerApps</tags>
    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework=".NETFramework4.8">
        <!-- Host version marker required by the Tool Library -->
        <dependency id="XrmToolBox" version="1.2025.10.74" />
      </group>
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="bin\Release\net48\PluginFailureCorrelationExplorer.dll" target="lib\net48\Plugins\PluginFailureCorrelationExplorer.dll" />
    <file src="..\..\README.md" target="docs\README.md" />
  </files>
</package>
